  camt.054.001.04 (ISO 20022 version 2013), the shape a Swiss bank delivers
  today. Structurally identical to a real Raiffeisen debit/credit notification;
  every name, address, IBAN and reference below is a PLACEHOLDER.

  The IBANs use IID 99999, which is not issued to any Swiss bank, so they can
  never collide with a real account. Their check digits are valid so that
  validate_iban() accepts them.

  Note the account IBAN is a NORMAL IBAN while the payment carries a QRR
  reference — exactly what a real file looks like, because the QR-IBAN is a
  separate number on the same account. The import must not reject this.
-->
